From: PowerVLC <powervlc@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] make BD-J network access configurable

BD-Live servers embedded in old discs are commonly gone or unresponsive. In
addition to the privacy problem of unexpected third-party connections, a
connection attempt can leave the menu on its loading screen indefinitely.

Add a player setting which rejects socket creation before any network traffic
occurs. Keep the standard player capability properties unchanged so discs can
run their normal offline fallback after the connection fails. Libbluray's own
default remains enabled for API compatibility; applications can make access
opt-in.
---
